                <pb facs="0284" n="196" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg196"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.6374/1173a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Culbertson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-06-24T15:00:00-04:00">June 24, 1933—3 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>33. Please send by first air mail latest available text of bill for reorganizing
                    nitrate industry. Communication just received from one of the interests
                    represented refers to “seventh and definitive draft” of which Department has no
                    copy. Keep Department currently advised by air mail of any changes in text.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
